## Primitives in the hydra.core.lib.literals module.
##
## Conversion and parse/print for literal values.
## The numeric conversion primitives (bigintToInt32, float64ToFloat32, ...) convert between Hydra's literal numeric types; lossless conversions are exact, and each lossy conversion states its truncation or rounding behavior in its own documentation.
## The parseX primitives are pure conversions from text to values, with an optional codomain wherever parsing can fail; the printX primitives are the pure conversions back from values to text.
module hydra.core.lib.literals

import hydra.core.paths
import hydra.core.ast
import hydra.core.coders
import hydra.core.model
import hydra.core.diff
import hydra.core.docs
import hydra.core.error.checking
import hydra.core.error.model
import hydra.core.error.file
import hydra.core.error.packaging
import hydra.core.error.system
import hydra.core.errors
import hydra.core.file
import hydra.core.graph
import hydra.core.json.model
import hydra.core.markdown
import hydra.core.packaging
import hydra.core.parsing
import hydra.core.query
import hydra.core.regex
import hydra.core.relational
import hydra.core.system
import hydra.core.tabular
import hydra.core.testing
import hydra.core.time
import hydra.core.topology
import hydra.core.typed
import hydra.core.typing
import hydra.core.util
import hydra.core.validation
import hydra.core.variants

## Decode a base64 ASCII string to binary data.
##
## base64ToBinary(s) decodes the standard base64 (RFC 4648) ASCII string s and returns the resulting bytes as binary data.
## Inverse of binaryToBase64: base64ToBinary(binaryToBase64(b)) is b for every binary value. Behavior on strings which are not valid base64 is host-defined.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.stringToBinary.
##
## @availableSince 0.18
## @requirement decodesStandardBase64 base64ToBinary decodes a standard base64 (RFC 4648) ASCII string to the binary data it represents, including the empty string decoding to empty binary data.
primitive base64ToBinary : ∀.string → binary

## Convert a bigint to a decimal.
##
## bigintToDecimal(x) returns the exact decimal representation of x. Since decimal is arbitrary-precision and bigint is also arbitrary-precision, the conversion is lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion bigintToDecimal returns the exact decimal representation of a bigint, with no precision loss, for positive, negative, and zero values.
primitive bigintToDecimal : ∀.bigint → decimal

## Convert a bigint to an int16 (truncating).
##
## bigintToInt16(x) returns x reduced modulo 2^16 and reinterpreted as a signed two's-complement int16. Values outside [-2^15, 2^15-1] wrap silently with no exception.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsInRange bigintToInt16 returns the int16 with the same numeric value as the bigint, for positive and negative values within the int16 range.
## @requirement wrapsTwosComplementOutOfRange bigintToInt16 on a value outside the int16 range ([-2^15, 2^15-1]) wraps silently to the corresponding two's-complement int16, with no exception, at both the positive and negative (all-bits-set) boundary.
primitive bigintToInt16 : ∀.bigint → int16

## Convert a bigint to an int32 (truncating).
##
## bigintToInt32(x) returns x reduced modulo 2^32 and reinterpreted as a signed two's-complement int32. Values outside [-2^31, 2^31-1] wrap silently with no exception.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsInRange bigintToInt32 returns the int32 with the same numeric value as the bigint, for positive and negative values within the int32 range.
## @requirement wrapsTwosComplementOutOfRange bigintToInt32 on a value outside the int32 range ([-2^31, 2^31-1]) wraps silently to the corresponding two's-complement int32, with no exception, at both the positive and negative (all-bits-set) boundary; this holds even on hosts where int32 is represented as a wider native integer, which must not skip the narrowing step.
primitive bigintToInt32 : ∀.bigint → int32

## Convert a bigint to an int64 (truncating).
##
## bigintToInt64(x) returns x reduced modulo 2^64 and reinterpreted as a signed two's-complement int64. Values outside [-2^63, 2^63-1] wrap silently with no exception.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsInRange bigintToInt64 returns the int64 with the same numeric value as the bigint, for positive and negative values within the int64 range.
primitive bigintToInt64 : ∀.bigint → int64

## Convert a bigint to an int8 (truncating).
##
## bigintToInt8(x) returns x reduced modulo 2^8 and reinterpreted as a signed two's-complement int8. Values outside [-128, 127] wrap silently with no exception.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsInRange bigintToInt8 returns the int8 with the same numeric value as the bigint, for positive and negative values within the int8 range.
## @requirement wrapsTwosComplementOutOfRange bigintToInt8 on a value outside the int8 range ([-128, 127]) wraps silently to the corresponding two's-complement int8, with no exception, at both the positive and negative (all-bits-set) boundary.
primitive bigintToInt8 : ∀.bigint → int8

## Convert a bigint to a uint16 (truncating).
##
## bigintToUint16(x) returns x reduced modulo 2^16 as an unsigned uint16. Values outside [0, 2^16-1] wrap silently with no exception.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsInRange bigintToUint16 returns the uint16 with the same numeric value as the bigint, for a zero or typical in-range value.
primitive bigintToUint16 : ∀.bigint → uint16

## Convert a bigint to a uint32 (truncating).
##
## bigintToUint32(x) returns x reduced modulo 2^32 as an unsigned uint32. Values outside [0, 2^32-1] wrap silently with no exception.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsInRange bigintToUint32 returns the uint32 with the same numeric value as the bigint, for a zero or typical in-range value.
primitive bigintToUint32 : ∀.bigint → uint32

## Convert a bigint to a uint64 (truncating).
##
## bigintToUint64(x) returns x reduced modulo 2^64 as an unsigned uint64. Values outside [0, 2^64-1] wrap silently with no exception.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsInRange bigintToUint64 returns the uint64 with the same numeric value as the bigint, for a zero or typical in-range value.
primitive bigintToUint64 : ∀.bigint → uint64

## Convert a bigint to a uint8 (truncating).
##
## bigintToUint8(x) returns x reduced modulo 2^8 as an unsigned uint8. Values outside [0, 255] wrap silently with no exception.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsInRange bigintToUint8 returns the uint8 with the same numeric value as the bigint, for a zero or typical in-range value.
primitive bigintToUint8 : ∀.bigint → uint8

## Encode binary data as a base64 ASCII string.
##
## binaryToBase64(b) encodes the bytes of b using standard base64 (RFC 4648) and returns the result as an ASCII string.
## Total and round-trippable: base64ToBinary(binaryToBase64(b)) is b for every binary value. Use this to embed arbitrary binary data in a string context (e.g. a JSON value). For interpreting bytes as text, use hydra.core.lib.text.decodeUtf8 instead.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.binaryToString.
##
## @availableSince 0.18
## @requirement encodesStandardBase64 binaryToBase64 encodes binary data as a standard base64 (RFC 4648) ASCII string, including empty binary data encoding to the empty string.
primitive binaryToBase64 : ∀.binary → string

## Convert binary data to a list of byte values.
##
## binaryToBytes(b) returns the bytes of b as an int32 list with values in [0, 255], preserving byte order.
## The result list element type is int32 rather than uint8 because Hydra's primitive collections work most naturally with int32 indices.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement returnsUnsignedByteValues binaryToBytes returns the bytes of the binary data as a list of int32 values in [0, 255], preserving byte order, including byte values above 127 (which remain unsigned, not reinterpreted as negative), and the empty list for empty binary data.
primitive binaryToBytes : ∀.binary → list<int32>

## Convert a decimal to a bigint (truncating).
##
## decimalToBigint(x) returns x truncated toward zero. Fractional parts are discarded.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsWholeNumbers decimalToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as a whole-number decimal, for positive, negative, and zero values.
## @requirement truncatesFractionTowardZero decimalToBigint on a decimal with a fractional part discards the fraction, truncating toward zero (rounding down for positive values, up for negative values), not rounding to nearest.
primitive decimalToBigint : ∀.decimal → bigint

## Convert a decimal to a float32.
##
## decimalToFloat32(x) returns the IEEE 754 binary32 value closest to x under roundTiesToEven. Values outside the float32 representable range overflow to ±∞. Subnormal precision loss is silent.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsExactlyRepresentableValues decimalToFloat32 returns the float32 value with the same numeric value as a decimal that is exactly representable in binary32, for zero and whole-number values.
primitive decimalToFloat32 : ∀.decimal → float32

## Convert a decimal to a float64.
##
## decimalToFloat64(x) returns the IEEE 754 binary64 value closest to x under roundTiesToEven. Values outside the float64 representable range overflow to ±∞. Subnormal precision loss is silent.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsExactlyRepresentableValues decimalToFloat64 returns the float64 value with the same numeric value as a decimal that is exactly representable in binary64, for zero and whole-number values.
primitive decimalToFloat64 : ∀.decimal → float64

## Convert a float32 to a decimal.
##
## float32ToDecimal(x) returns the exact decimal representation of the binary32 value x. Special float32 values (±∞, NaN) have a host-defined decimal representation; finite values convert exactly since binary32 values are dyadic rationals.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsExactlyRepresentableValues float32ToDecimal returns the exact decimal representation of a binary32 value, for zero and whole-number values.
primitive float32ToDecimal : ∀.float32 → decimal

## Convert a float32 to a float64.
##
## float32ToFloat64(x) returns the binary64 value with the same numeric value as x; ±∞ and NaN pass through. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessWidening float32ToFloat64 returns the float64 value with the same numeric value as a float32, with no precision loss, for positive, negative, and zero values.
primitive float32ToFloat64 : ∀.float32 → float64

## Convert a float64 to a decimal.
##
## float64ToDecimal(x) returns the exact decimal representation of the binary64 value x. Special float64 values (±∞, NaN) have a host-defined decimal representation; finite values convert exactly since binary64 values are dyadic rationals.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsExactlyRepresentableValues float64ToDecimal returns the exact decimal representation of a binary64 value, for zero and whole-number values.
primitive float64ToDecimal : ∀.float64 → decimal

## Convert a float64 to a float32 (lossy).
##
## float64ToFloat32(x) returns the binary32 value closest to x under roundTiesToEven. Values outside the binary32 range overflow to ±∞; subnormal precision loss is silent; NaN payload may be canonicalized by the host.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement convertsExactlyRepresentableValues float64ToFloat32 returns the float32 value with the same numeric value as a float64 that is exactly representable in binary32, for positive, negative, and zero values.
primitive float64ToFloat32 : ∀.float64 → float32

## Convert an int16 to a bigint.
##
## int16ToBigint(x) returns the bigint with the same numeric value as x. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion int16ToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as the int16, with no precision loss, for positive and negative values.
primitive int16ToBigint : ∀.int16 → bigint

## Convert an int32 to a bigint.
##
## int32ToBigint(x) returns the bigint with the same numeric value as x. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion int32ToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as the int32, with no precision loss, for positive, negative, and zero values.
primitive int32ToBigint : ∀.int32 → bigint

## Convert an int64 to a bigint.
##
## int64ToBigint(x) returns the bigint with the same numeric value as x. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion int64ToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as the int64, with no precision loss, for positive and negative values.
primitive int64ToBigint : ∀.int64 → bigint

## Convert an int8 to a bigint.
##
## int8ToBigint(x) returns the bigint with the same numeric value as x. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion int8ToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as the int8, with no precision loss, for positive and negative values including the int8 min/max boundary.
primitive int8ToBigint : ∀.int8 → bigint

## Parse a string as a bigint.
##
## parseBigint(s) returns Just(x) where x is the bigint parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid bigint literal.
## Accepted syntax follows the Haskell Show/Read convention: an optional leading minus sign followed by a sequence of decimal digits. Whitespace is not stripped; leading or trailing whitespace causes parse failure.
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readBigint.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseBigint returns the bigint parsed from a valid bigint literal, wrapped, for positive, negative, zero, and arbitrarily large values.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidInput parseBigint returns none when the string is not a valid bigint literal.
primitive parseBigint : ∀.string → optional<bigint>

## Parse a string as a boolean.
##
## parseBoolean(s) returns Just(true) for "true", Just(false) for "false", and Nothing for any other input (including "True"/"False" with capital initial letter on some hosts; behavior on capitalized forms is host-defined and should not be relied upon).
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readBoolean.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesExactLowercaseLiterals parseBoolean returns the wrapped boolean true for the exact string "true" and false for "false".
## @requirement noneOnInvalidInput parseBoolean returns none for any string other than the exact lowercase literals "true" or "false".
primitive parseBoolean : ∀.string → optional<boolean>

## Parse a string as a decimal.
##
## parseDecimal(s) returns Just(x) where x is the decimal parsed from s, or Nothing on parse failure.
## Accepted syntax is the standard decimal literal: an optional sign, an integer part, an optional fractional part, and an optional exponent (e.g. -1.5, 2e10, 0.0).
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readDecimal.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseDecimal returns the decimal parsed from a valid decimal literal, wrapped, for positive, negative, and zero values.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidInput parseDecimal returns none when the string is not a valid decimal literal.
primitive parseDecimal : ∀.string → optional<decimal>

## Parse a string as a float32.
##
## parseFloat32(s) returns Just(x) where x is the IEEE 754 binary32 value closest to the number parsed from s under roundTiesToEven, or Nothing on parse failure.
## Accepted special-value literals ("NaN", "Infinity", "-Infinity", etc.) and their capitalization are host-defined.
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readFloat32.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseFloat32 returns the float32 value closest to the number parsed from a valid literal, wrapped, for positive and negative values.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidInput parseFloat32 returns none when the string is not a valid float literal.
primitive parseFloat32 : ∀.string → optional<float32>

## Parse a string as a float64.
##
## parseFloat64(s) returns Just(x) where x is the IEEE 754 binary64 value closest to the number parsed from s under roundTiesToEven, or Nothing on parse failure.
## Accepted special-value literals ("NaN", "Infinity", "-Infinity", etc.) and their capitalization are host-defined.
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readFloat64.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseFloat64 returns the float64 value closest to the number parsed from a valid literal, wrapped, for positive and negative values.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidInput parseFloat64 returns none when the string is not a valid float literal.
primitive parseFloat64 : ∀.string → optional<float64>

## Parse a string as an int16.
##
## parseInt16(s) returns Just(x) where x is the int16 parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid integer literal or the parsed value is outside [-2^15, 2^15-1].
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readInt16.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseInt16 returns the int16 parsed from a valid integer literal within range, wrapped, for positive and negative values.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidInput parseInt16 returns none when the string is not a valid integer literal.
primitive parseInt16 : ∀.string → optional<int16>

## Parse a string as an int32.
##
## parseInt32(s) returns Just(x) where x is the int32 parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid integer literal or the parsed value is outside [-2^31, 2^31-1].
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readInt32.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseInt32 returns the int32 parsed from a valid integer literal within range, wrapped, for positive and negative values.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidInput parseInt32 returns none when the string is not a valid integer literal.
primitive parseInt32 : ∀.string → optional<int32>

## Parse a string as an int64.
##
## parseInt64(s) returns Just(x) where x is the int64 parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid integer literal or the parsed value is outside [-2^63, 2^63-1].
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readInt64.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseInt64 returns the int64 parsed from a valid integer literal within range, wrapped, for positive and negative values.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidInput parseInt64 returns none when the string is not a valid integer literal.
primitive parseInt64 : ∀.string → optional<int64>

## Parse a string as an int8.
##
## parseInt8(s) returns Just(x) where x is the int8 parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid integer literal or the parsed value is outside [-128, 127].
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readInt8.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseInt8 returns the int8 parsed from a valid integer literal within range, wrapped, for positive and negative values including the int8 min/max boundary.
## @requirement noneOnOutOfRangeOrInvalidInput parseInt8 returns none when the string is not a valid integer literal, or when the parsed value is outside the int8 range [-128, 127].
primitive parseInt8 : ∀.string → optional<int8>

## Parse a string-literal token to a plain string (Just) or Nothing on parse failure.
##
## parseString(s) parses s as a Haskell-syntax string literal token: an opening double-quote, escaped characters per the Haskell lexical grammar (backslash escapes for special characters and Unicode code points), and a closing double-quote. Returns Just of the decoded payload on success or Nothing on malformed input.
## Total. The inverse of printString.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readString.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesQuotedLiterals parseString returns the decoded payload of a double-quoted string literal, wrapped.
## @requirement noneOnUnquotedInput parseString returns none when the string is not a well-formed double-quoted string literal (for example, an unquoted bare string).
primitive parseString : ∀.string → optional<string>

## Parse a string as a uint16.
##
## parseUint16(s) returns Just(x) where x is the uint16 parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid non-negative integer literal or the parsed value is outside [0, 2^16-1].
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readUint16.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseUint16 returns the uint16 parsed from a valid non-negative integer literal within range, wrapped.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidOrNegativeInput parseUint16 returns none when the string is not a valid integer literal, or when it represents a negative value.
primitive parseUint16 : ∀.string → optional<uint16>

## Parse a string as a uint32.
##
## parseUint32(s) returns Just(x) where x is the uint32 parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid non-negative integer literal or the parsed value is outside [0, 2^32-1].
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readUint32.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseUint32 returns the uint32 parsed from a valid non-negative integer literal within range, wrapped, including at the maximum representable value (2^32-1).
## @requirement noneOnInvalidOrNegativeInput parseUint32 returns none when the string is not a valid integer literal, or when it represents a negative value.
## @requirement noneOnOverflow parseUint32 returns none when the parsed value exceeds the uint32 maximum (2^32-1), one past the boundary.
primitive parseUint32 : ∀.string → optional<uint32>

## Parse a string as a uint64.
##
## parseUint64(s) returns Just(x) where x is the uint64 parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid non-negative integer literal or the parsed value is outside [0, 2^64-1].
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readUint64.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseUint64 returns the uint64 parsed from a valid non-negative integer literal within range, wrapped, including large in-range values.
## @requirement noneOnInvalidOrNegativeInput parseUint64 returns none when the string is not a valid integer literal, or when it represents a negative value.
## @requirement noneOnOverflow parseUint64 returns none when the parsed value exceeds the uint64 maximum (2^64-1), one past the boundary.
primitive parseUint64 : ∀.string → optional<uint64>

## Parse a string as a uint8.
##
## parseUint8(s) returns Just(x) where x is the uint8 parsed from s, or Nothing if s is not a valid non-negative integer literal or the parsed value is outside [0, 255].
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.readUint8.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement parsesValidLiterals parseUint8 returns the uint8 parsed from a valid non-negative integer literal within range, wrapped, including at the maximum representable value (255).
## @requirement noneOnInvalidOrNegativeInput parseUint8 returns none when the string is not a valid integer literal, or when it represents a negative value.
primitive parseUint8 : ∀.string → optional<uint8>

## Render a bigint as a string.
##
## printBigint(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x: an optional leading minus sign followed by decimal digits. No leading zeros are produced (except for the value 0 itself, which renders as "0").
## Total. The inverse of parseBigint.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showBigint.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printBigint renders a bigint as its canonical decimal string, with a leading minus sign for negative values and no leading sign for positive values or zero.
primitive printBigint : ∀.bigint → string

## Render a boolean as a string.
##
## printBoolean(true) = "true"; printBoolean(false) = "false".
## Total. The inverse of parseBoolean.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showBoolean.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersLowercaseLiterals printBoolean renders true as the exact string "true" and false as "false".
primitive printBoolean : ∀.boolean → string

## Render a decimal as a string.
##
## printDecimal(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x as a string. The exact form (use of scientific notation, trailing zeros, etc.) is host-defined but always round-trips with parseDecimal.
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showDecimal.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printDecimal renders a decimal as a string, for positive and negative whole and fractional values, that always round-trips through parseDecimal back to the original value.
primitive printDecimal : ∀.decimal → string

## Render a float32 as a string.
##
## printFloat32(x) returns a string representation of x. Finite values use the shortest decimal that round-trips through parseFloat32 back to x. Special values render as "NaN", "Infinity", or "-Infinity" (capitalization is host-defined).
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showFloat32.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersRoundTrippableRepresentation printFloat32 renders a float32 as a string, for positive, negative, zero, and small-magnitude values, that round-trips through parseFloat32 back to the original value.
primitive printFloat32 : ∀.float32 → string

## Render a float64 as a string.
##
## printFloat64(x) returns a string representation of x. Finite values use the shortest decimal that round-trips through parseFloat64 back to x. Special values render as "NaN", "Infinity", or "-Infinity" (capitalization is host-defined).
## Total.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showFloat64.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersRoundTrippableRepresentation printFloat64 renders a float64 as a string, for positive, zero, and small-magnitude values, that round-trips through parseFloat64 back to the original value.
primitive printFloat64 : ∀.float64 → string

## Render an int16 as a string.
##
## printInt16(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x: an optional leading minus sign followed by decimal digits.
## Total. The inverse of parseInt16.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showInt16.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printInt16 renders an int16 as its canonical decimal string, with a leading minus sign for negative values.
primitive printInt16 : ∀.int16 → string

## Render an int32 as a string.
##
## printInt32(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x: an optional leading minus sign followed by decimal digits.
## Total. The inverse of parseInt32.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showInt32.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printInt32 renders an int32 as its canonical decimal string, with a leading minus sign for negative values and no sign for zero.
primitive printInt32 : ∀.int32 → string

## Render an int64 as a string.
##
## printInt64(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x: an optional leading minus sign followed by decimal digits.
## Total. The inverse of parseInt64.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showInt64.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printInt64 renders an int64 as its canonical decimal string, with a leading minus sign for negative values.
primitive printInt64 : ∀.int64 → string

## Render an int8 as a string.
##
## printInt8(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x: an optional leading minus sign followed by decimal digits.
## Total. The inverse of parseInt8.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showInt8.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printInt8 renders an int8 as its canonical decimal string, with a leading minus sign for negative values.
primitive printInt8 : ∀.int8 → string

## Render a string as a string-literal token (escaped and quoted).
##
## printString(s) returns a Haskell-syntax string literal token representing s: an opening double-quote, the characters of s with special characters escaped (backslash sequences for control characters, quotes, and non-printable Unicode code points), and a closing double-quote.
## Total. The inverse of parseString.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showString.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement quotesAndPassesThroughPlainCharacters printString wraps a string in double quotes, passing plain ASCII characters through unescaped, for the empty string and ordinary text.
## @requirement escapesNonAsciiAsDecimalCodes printString renders every non-ASCII character as a backslash followed by its decimal Unicode code point, whether the character appears alone, mixed with ASCII text, or repeated.
## @requirement escapesNamedControlCharacters printString renders the characters with standard Haskell-syntax named escapes (tab, newline, carriage return, backslash, double quote, NUL, bell, backspace, form feed, vertical tab, delete) using their named escape form, not a raw or decimal-code representation.
primitive printString : ∀.string → string

## Render a uint16 as a string.
##
## printUint16(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x.
## Total. The inverse of parseUint16.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showUint16.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printUint16 renders a uint16 as its canonical unsigned decimal string, for zero and typical values.
primitive printUint16 : ∀.uint16 → string

## Render a uint32 as a string.
##
## printUint32(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x.
## Total. The inverse of parseUint32.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showUint32.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printUint32 renders a uint32 as its canonical unsigned decimal string, for zero and typical values.
primitive printUint32 : ∀.uint32 → string

## Render a uint64 as a string.
##
## printUint64(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x.
## Total. The inverse of parseUint64.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showUint64.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printUint64 renders a uint64 as its canonical unsigned decimal string, for zero and typical values.
primitive printUint64 : ∀.uint64 → string

## Render a uint8 as a string.
##
## printUint8(x) returns the canonical decimal representation of x.
## Total. The inverse of parseUint8.
## Renamed from hydra.lib.literals.showUint8.
##
## @availableSince 0.17.6
## @requirement rendersCanonicalDecimal printUint8 renders a uint8 as its canonical unsigned decimal string, for zero and the maximum representable value (255).
primitive printUint8 : ∀.uint8 → string

## Convert a uint16 to a bigint.
##
## uint16ToBigint(x) returns the bigint with the same numeric value as x. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion uint16ToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as the uint16, with no precision loss, for zero and typical in-range values.
primitive uint16ToBigint : ∀.uint16 → bigint

## Convert a uint32 to a bigint.
##
## uint32ToBigint(x) returns the bigint with the same numeric value as x. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion uint32ToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as the uint32, with no precision loss, for zero and typical in-range values.
primitive uint32ToBigint : ∀.uint32 → bigint

## Convert a uint64 to a bigint.
##
## uint64ToBigint(x) returns the bigint with the same numeric value as x. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion uint64ToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as the uint64, with no precision loss, for zero and typical in-range values.
primitive uint64ToBigint : ∀.uint64 → bigint

## Convert a uint8 to a bigint.
##
## uint8ToBigint(x) returns the bigint with the same numeric value as x. The conversion is exact and lossless.
## Total.
##
## @availableSince 0.15
## @requirement losslessConversion uint8ToBigint returns the bigint with the same numeric value as the uint8, with no precision loss, for zero and the maximum representable value (255).
primitive uint8ToBigint : ∀.uint8 → bigint